## 🛑 STOP Protocol — If Cost Detected

If implementing a feature would require a paid service:

```
🛑 COST DETECTED: [Feature] cannot be done for $0 using [service].

Reason: [why it would cost money]

Free alternatives:
A) [Alternative 1] — $0 because [reason] — Tradeoffs: [list]
B) [Alternative 2] — $0 because [reason] — Tradeoffs: [list]
C) Defer this feature until a free solution exists

Recommendation: [A / B / C] — because [reason]

Do NOT proceed until user confirms a free path.
```

**NEVER add a paid service as a temporary solution.**
**NEVER assume "we'll deal with billing later."**

---

## Supabase Quota Safety Rules

Supabase free tier limits to stay within:
- **Database**: 500MB — normalize data, no duplicate storage, no blobs in DB
- **Storage**: 1GB — compress images before upload, user avatars max 200KB
- **Auth MAU**: 50,000 — no concern for personal site
- **Bandwidth**: 2GB/mo — serve static assets via Cloudflare CDN, not Supabase
- **Edge Functions**: 500,000 invocations/mo — use sparingly, prefer static/SSG

### DB Efficiency Rules
- Never store large text blobs in DB — use markdown files in repo for blog/notes
- Never store base64 images in DB — use Supabase Storage with public bucket
- Use pagination — never fetch entire tables
- Add indexes on columns used in `WHERE`/`ORDER BY`
- Soft delete with `is_deleted` flag — never bulk delete and re-insert

---

## Bandwidth Conservation Rules
- All static assets (images, fonts, JS) served from Cloudflare CDN (free)
- Blog/notes content = markdown files in repo = static, $0 bandwidth from Supabase
- Supabase is called only for: auth, user data, game scores, bookmarks
- No polling — use Supabase Realtime only if absolutely necessary (counts toward bandwidth)
- Images: Use `<Image>` from Astro with width/height specified, WebP format

---

## Monetization Hooks (Future)
When monetization is added in future:
- Research free tier of monetization platform first (e.g., Stripe has no monthly fee — only % per transaction ✅)
- Design so monetization is opt-in and does not increase baseline infra cost
- Never add a service "just in case" — add only when actively needed

---

## Prohibited Services (Require Credit Card or Have No Free Tier)
- ❌ AWS, GCP, Azure (free tiers expire after 12 months or require card)
- ❌ Vercel (hobby free tier has bandwidth limits that require upgrade)
- ❌ PlanetScale (no longer has a free tier as of 2024)
- ❌ Heroku (removed free tier)
- ❌ MongoDB Atlas (requires card even on free tier)
- ❌ SendGrid / Mailgun (requires card for free tier in many regions)
- ❌ Any service with "Start free trial" instead of "Free forever"
